   "etymology": "From older mbëledh, from Old Albanian ënbëljedh, made of a prefix ënbë- of disputed origin + a component ljedh from Proto-Indo-European *leǵ- (“to gather”) (compare Latin legere, Ancient Greek λέγω (légō)). For the identity of ënbë-:\n* Orel reconstructs Proto-Albanian *ambi-ledza, thuse relating the prefix to Proto-Indo-European *h₂m̥bʰí (“around, towards”).\n* Demiraj reconstructs Proto-Albanian *əmbər-lʲę́ð(ə)-, from Pre-Proto-Albanian *ana-pra- + léj́i/a-, implying the prefix to be from an Albanian reflex of the root that gives Ancient Greek ἀνά (aná, “up, on”) + πρό (pró, “forward”).",
